Use resource and reserve categories through their complete definitions and evidence (@mine-classification: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mining-and-mineral-engineering, #source "../sources/Resource-and-Reserve-Reporting-CRIRSCO-CBRR.lingua#r_2CZZ64T1W8VC542VCNCH2E6DSR", #source "../sources/Hard-Rock-Miners-Handbook.lingua#r_18YBY5XX4TFS7ZQSKTQMW34EFA", #source "../sources/Penn-State-Introduction-to-Mining.lingua#r_5NAY6K47Y4Y61V4JF74JJNV4Q2", #mining-and-mineral-engineering "../../../../nature/earth/mineralogy-and-petrology/applications/Grain-associations-liberation-and-process-mineralogy.lingua#r_03BD9ADDV2B62T8RF26S61R77C") { r_752AR316YAX12F1XBWQ5E6B0B8
**Read:** [Resources, reserves, and technical-study definitions — CRIRSCO and CBRR](../sources/Resource-and-Reserve-Reporting-CRIRSCO-CBRR.lingua#r_2CZZ64T1W8VC542VCNCH2E6DSR), the complete template and guide; [Hard Rock Miner’s Handbook — Jack de la Vergne, fifth edition](../sources/Hard-Rock-Miners-Handbook.lingua#r_18YBY5XX4TFS7ZQSKTQMW34EFA), the full evaluation/reserve discussion with dated conventions distinguished; [Introduction to Mining Engineering — Penn State MNG 230](../sources/Penn-State-Introduction-to-Mining.lingua#r_5NAY6K47Y4Y61V4JF74JJNV4Q2), the complete evaluation and technical-study sequence.

Exploration targets/results, mineral resources, and mineral reserves describe different claims under identified reporting standards. Read the actual definitions, confidence, modifying factors, study scope, responsibilities, and evidence. A teaching calculation of grade times volume does not itself establish any category.

Reserve conversion connects geological confidence with technical, processing, economic, environmental, social, legal, infrastructural, and other relevant factors under the chosen framework. A factor is not satisfied merely because a report includes its heading. Feasibility evidence and uncertainty should be traceable to the particular proposal and date.

Distinguish a conceptual/scoping comparison, a pre-feasibility study, a feasibility study, an operating plan, and a public reporting statement. Their purposes, assumptions, detail, confidence, and requirements differ. The CRIRSCO template is advisory for code development/comparison; applicable national/regional rules require their own identified current source.

**Work:** read the full 2024 template and 2022 Portuguese CBRR guide, preserving their roles/versions. Reconstruct an authorized public technical claim's evidence chain and identify unresolved factors. Compare two studies whose tonnage/grade labels look similar but whose supports, assumptions, or reporting categories differ.

Follow [Relate mineral associations to liberation without mistaking a section for every particle](../../../../nature/earth/mineralogy-and-petrology/applications/Grain-associations-liberation-and-process-mineralogy.lingua#r_03BD9ADDV2B62T8RF26S61R77C) for the shared mineral-association and process-mineralogy step. Its mining continuation returns to geometallurgical interpretation, connecting geological inventory with the behavior actually relevant to extraction and concentration.

